    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0100" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg30"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Van
                        Valkenburgh</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 28, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your telegram dated
                    February 22d, announcing the departure of two commissioners and suite, appointed
                    by the Tycoon to visit Washington on business mentioned in your despatch No. 43.
                    Information has also been received by the department of the arrival of the
                    commissioners at San Francisco, and of their intention to leave there for New
                    York on the 1st of next month. In that city they will be properly received by an
                    officer of this department.</p>
                <p>Your despatches No. 43 and 45 have been communicated to the Secretary of the
                    Navy.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. B. Van Valkenburgh,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
